{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning. I'll just do your observations before the doctor calls you. Could you pop your arm out?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, fine. Been sat out there ages though. Forty minutes and I'm shattered.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): Sorry about the wait. Blood pressure is 122 over 78, pulse 92, temperature 36.7, oxygen 99 percent, and breathing 16. Right, the doctor's free now.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (DOCTOR): Hello, I'm Dr Shah. Come through. What's been going on?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): There's a lump. In my neck. Been there three weeks and I'm sick of looking at it.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (DOCTOR): A lump in the neck for three weeks. Which side, and does it hurt when you touch it?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): The cat did it. Mabel. Scratched my hand to bits, little menace, and I'm too tired for this.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): We'll get to the cat in a moment. The lump, which side is it, and is it painful?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Right side. And no, it doesn't hurt. Not sore at all.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): Has it got any bigger over those three weeks?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really. Same sort of size. I've been proper knackered for weeks as well.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh, and I woke up drenched one night. Sheets were damp. Just the once, not every night.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): Once only. Any cough?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): And fever, any fever with that or now?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Not that either.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): Have you lost any weight?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm, not really. Well, actually, my jeans are hanging off a bit. I haven't weighed myself so I don't know.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): All right, we'll leave the weight as unsure. Any long-term conditions I should know about?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Asthma. Had it since I was little. Still got it.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): Still got the asthma. What inhalers are you using?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Blue one, salbutermol, two puffs if I need them. And clenil, the brown one, two puffs morning and night. I think the clenil is 100, or is it 200, I always mix them up.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): So salbutamol when required, and Clenil twice a day, though you're not sure if that's 100 or 200 micrograms. Any wheeze from the asthma just lately?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Well, sometimes, if I've legged it for the bus. Not all the time.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sometimes on exertion, not constant. When was that cat scratch?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Err, since Diwali or after. Or maybe before, I can't remember. The days all blur.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (DOCTOR): You can't date the scratch. Has the wound healed?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah it's just a mark now. Scab's gone.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): Let me have a look at your neck and your hand, and listen to your chest.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (DOCTOR): There's a smooth lump on the right side of the neck, about two centimetres, mobile, skin over it looks normal, and it's not tender. The scratch mark on the left hand is healed. Chest is clear, no wheeze today.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): I think this is most likely a reactive lymph node. Cat scratch disease is possible given the scratch, but I can't exclude other causes yet.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'd like to organise blood tests, a full blood count and a CRP, and an ultrasound of the neck. The nurse can take the bloods after we've finished.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): More waiting. Brilliant. Do I have to come back as well?",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (DOCTOR): Yes, we'll book you back in a fortnight for the results. If the lump grows quickly or you feel properly unwell, come back sooner rather than waiting.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Fine. Can I go and get the bloods then? I need a coffee.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (NURSE): I'll take you through for the bloods now. Full blood count and CRP, was it?"
 ],
